※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4570

※ The same escape, one level of indirection out.  `rr` names the place `r1` is,
※ so writing through it puts a reference where `r1` holds one -- and `r1` lasts
※ as long as the body while `v2` lasts as long as the arm.  What is asked of a
※ name is asked of a place that holds a reference, and how long that place lasts
※ is how long what names it does.

let b1 : bool = true

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u6:
    let v1 : mut u32 = 0u32
    let r1 : mut &mut u32 = &v1
    let rr : &mut &mut u32 = &mut r1
    if b1:
        let v2 : mut u32 = 1u32
        rr⌖ ← &v2
    if rr⌖⌖ = 0u32 { 0u6 } else { 1u6 }
